# 2026-11-16 Interrupted terminal paste
Source review confirms the terminal's five-second idle warning begins with
Esc: recover paste. Describe one new Escape after that warning to recover the
retained draft, then review and deliberate Enter to send. Escape bytes before
the warning must keep paste mode active; verify the final correction before
publication. Recovery neither submits nor cancels an
in-flight answer. Keep this separate from browser controls and preserve the
matching-release publication hold; the observed PTY check is not phone use.

# 2026-11-16 Terminal input qualification
Limit pasted-newline protection to a recognized paste boundary. Explain that
severely delayed or damaged terminal controls can be treated as typing, cause
submission or consume a character. Give the verified fresh-Escape-and-pause
recovery with its normal cancel/draft effects; do not expose protocol bytes,
private source references or claim complete prevention. Keep public release
gates and the distinction from browser controls unchanged.

# 2026-11-16 Home and End controls
Source review confirms Home and End navigate the chat history only with an
empty draft. With a nonempty draft they move to the start or end of that
draft. Keep the public keyboard description conditional on the draft state.

# 2026-11-24 Release reconciliation
Supersedes dated independence, temporary-only memory, 1000-character, Public web picker and no-actions notes above. Public guide describes released remembered private conversations, Org + web, 50000-character composer, two concurrent asks, brain-written reply chips, /model /deep /charter /guide /mandate /checkins, task links, explicit confirmation and current mandate enforcement. Short callbacks are distinguished from Agenda work; a durable scheduled receipt is required, and live delivery is not certified. New image attachment, registry availability/ranking, unlimited quota and progress-recovery changes remain feature-branch work and are excluded until matching release. Rewrite-only public surface; no source identifiers, deployment detail, private excerpts or roadmap promises.

# Final prose review
Use a verified timing suffix without extra words after the duration. Describe
network commands as unavailable while asks are pending, not queued. Existing
dated history is retained only as history; current gotchas match the guide.

# Retained terminal controls
Keep the existing independently described terminal commands, keyboard and paste
recovery instructions. Their question-only /web behavior is not the browser
Org + web contract. Preserve the private-chat/shared-note and provider boundary.

# 2026-11-24 Model, image and progress help draft
Prepare reader-facing daily allowance, authoritative model availability and
Auto configured-preference guidance from current labels. Document retrying
observed progress, up to four JPEG/PNG/WebP images with 2 MiB combined prepared
bytes, request-only image retention and public-web/delayed-action boundaries.
Use only source-supported in-number/from-now and middle-delay read examples.
A due receipt proves storage, not due delivery. This feature-branch draft stays
unpublished until matching rollout verification; never promise general timed
actions or callback success. Keep public prose free of private source details.

# 2026-11-26 Ask for work: requested changes, follow line, change cards
Checked against the released browser and brain behaviour (2026-11-26).
Public guide now says: drafts the person asked for in their own words
confirm themselves through their own signed-in session; deletes, schedule
deletes, sprint rollovers and anything marked permanent wait 5 s behind
Stop; drafts not asked for, drafts whose instructions mention secrets or
sending data out, restored drafts and runs of an existing task still show
a card (Run now opens the Agenda in front to confirm). One tap: cancel a
task, pause a schedule, raise a priority; two taps: create a task, sprint
rollover, permanent delete. Mandate starts from Brain Talk work only for
the grantor or an org owner/admin and run as the grantor; others see Not
started automatically. A follow line tracks created-and-queued and
mandate-started runs (not scheduled ones) for up to 45 minutes. The person
a run ran as can get a run-finished message; other askers are not told.
Agents asking through tools always get a card. The owner's live check of
auto-confirm is still open; keep wording conditional on what the screen
shows. Image limit unchanged: the released composer still caps four images
at 2 MiB combined, although the server accepts larger requests.
- 2026-11-27: org policy is on from the start (owner steward, every kind, no limits, revoke stays revoked); questions go to the org brain first (friendly agent, via brain, 4 h default). Merge at release of the default policy and friendly agent branches.
